we still know very little about what's  in store for 2021's new ghostbusters  sequel ghostbusters afterlife but we're  very excited about what's next here's  what we know so far about director jason  reitman's foray into a new neighborhood  with something strange  the first reports of jason reitman's  involvement in a new ghostbusters film  arrived in january 2019. reitman soon  confirmed via his twitter account that  the film would hit theaters on july 10th  2020. then covet 19 happened and  ghostbusters afterlife has been moved  back multiple times since the film was  initially bumped to march 5th 2021 then  a new release date of june 11 2021 was  set after those both fell through sony  moved the release date back first to  november 11th then to november 19th that  would seem to be the date that will  finally stick it seems like a lifetime  ago now but when the initial teaser that  announced the film dropped in january  2019 didn't give a title fans simply  started referring to the upcoming film  as ghostbusters 2020 assuming that the  movie would actually come out that year  the title remained a mystery until  december 2019 when the british board of  film classification which has to approve  all trailers in the uk revealed that the  approval notice for the new trailer gave  the title ghostbusters afterlife it's an  appropriate title given that the film is  not only about ghosts but also about  legacy  reitman has noted that his idea for the  film began with a 12 year old girl  carrying a proton pack and that image  ultimately expanded to include a whole  family that 12 year old phoebe will be  played by mckenna grace a rising young  talent who's been seen in everything  from captain marvel to chilling  adventures of sabrina to the haunting of  hill house carrie [ __ ] who's shown her  talents in tv series like fargo and the  leftovers as well as films like gone  girl and avengers infinity war plays  phoebe's mother callie finn wolfhard  who's probably best known for stranger  things and the it movies plays phoebe's  brother trevor in september 2019  producer ivan reichman revealed comedy  superstar turned superhero paul rudd's  role in the film saying he's a  seismologist who's come to this small  town because they've been having  mysterious earthquakes the earthquakes  are likely tied to paranormal events  rudd's character mr gruberson also ends  up working as a summer school teacher  likely creating his connection with the  family at the film's center  in june 2019 sigourney weaver seemed to  confirm in an interview that she was  indeed reprising her role as dana  barrett she said it's going to be crazy  working with the guys again either i  have a monster in my kitchen or i'm  completely crazy  i don't think you're crazy  oh good that makes me feel so much  better those guys  are obviously bill murray dan aykroyd  and ernie hudson aykroyd confirmed in  september 2019 that he would be  returning to the franchise along with  most of the original people by the end  of 2019 murray hudson and annie potts  were also all confirmed to be on board  in early 2020 vanity fair ran a report  from the set of afterlife while the  publication was strictly banned from  revealing anything about the plot an  extended conversation with murray  confirmed that something special was in  store for the iconic characters he said  the script is good it's got lots of  emotion in it it's got lots of family in  it with through lines that are really  interesting it's gonna work  jason reitman's feature film directorial  career began in 2005 with thank you for  smoking since then he's become known for  a particular style that often walks the  line between comedy and drama in films  like juno up in the air tully young  adult and most recently the front runner  his films are often small in scale  exploring the intimacy and absurdity of  human relationships rather than big set  pieces his comedy usually comes out of  interaction between characters rather  than gangs though he's undoubtedly  formed his own writing and directing  style reitman's interest in filmmaking  has its roots in family he's the son of  actress genevieve robert and writer  director ivan reitman who notably  directed the original ghostbusters and  ghostbusters 2. the ghostbusters  franchise is an integral part of jason  reitman's life he even had a cameo in  the 1989's ghostbusters 2 when he was  around 11 years old  you know my dad said you guys are full  of crap a sci-fi comedy about ghost  hunters isn't exactly in line with his  previous films but when it was announced  that he would helm afterlife his  familial ties to the franchise helped it  all make sense  it took a while to see more than a few  images related to reitman's new take on  ghostbusters and what we did see  consistently leaned heavily on nostalgia  the first teaser begins with a wide shot  of a large metal building in the middle  of a wooded area the camera pushes in  closer and closer to the door eventually  revealing the ghostbusters old ride  ecto-1 just sitting in storage the first  real trailer arrived in early december  2019. it largely follows the two kids at  the heart of the story trevor and phoebe  as they get used to their new life at  their inherited farmhouse in a small  oklahoma town but things get weird when  an eerie green light starts to emit from  an old pit outside of town mr gruberson  explains they're also experiencing weird  seismic activity that there's no logical  explanation for then the kids finally  bring an old ghost trap they found in  their farmhouse school and mr gruberson  realizes they must have a connection to  the ghostbusters it's revealed that  there hasn't been a real ghost sighting  in three decades and the ghostbusters  once regarded as heroes are now  forgotten legends phoebe and trevor  begin to seek out more information about  their long-lost grandfather who owned  the farmhouse the trailer reveals he was  indeed dr egon spengler one of the  original ghostbusters while the trailer  doesn't have any new footage of the  returning ghostbusters cast it does  provide a nostalgic kick by playing bill  murray's speech about fate from the 1984  original call it  faith call it lock call it karma  i believe that everything happens for a  reason the second trailer released in  july 2021 has much of the same material  as the first but it does include a scene  with annie potts's janine melnitz and a  quick look at the arms of what  definitely seems to be dr raymond's  stance rey appears to have some numbers  tattooed on one of his arms and jason  reitman told ign that the numbers  referenced the conversation about  judgment day between rey and winston  zetamor from the first film i remember  revelation 7 12  and i looked as he opened the sixth seal  and behold there was a great earthquake  for jason reitman's planned sequel  recreating the same look and feel he  remembered from the original films was  important with his father's connections  to the beginnings of the franchise he  had the resources to make it all work  the younger reitman went to great  lengths to replicate key details from  the 1980s for the sequel up to and  including finding the original letters  used to make the film's posters he  explained on bill burr's monday morning  podcast we went back to the work files  for the sound of the proton pack and we  went back to the stems of elmer  bernstein's score we went back and found  the original physical vinyl letters they  used to create the ghostbusters poster  in 1984. we shot physical titles with a  light and smoke effect because that's  how they would have done it back in the  day when reitman sat down with ign to  break down the second trailer he said  that instead of trying to mimic the  aesthetic of the original films using  modern day visual effects he and his  team went right back to the source he  said we actually found the original  special effects 70 millimeter footage  and scanned it 